WEBVTT

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.760
So, when my tinnitus started,
I just thought I was going crazy.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.739
I didn't know what it was,
there was just terrible hissing

00:00:08.779 --> 00:00:15.260
and buzzing noises in both of my ears
and it was driving me insane.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.840
I was angry all the time
and so my ulcers started

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.340
flaring up and I had
terrible stomach pain.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.893
So, fortunately, I went to my doctor
for stomach pain and ended

00:00:26.933 --> 00:00:31.506
up mentioning the ringing in my ears,
which he explained to me was

00:00:31.546 --> 00:00:37.460
tinnitus and he sent me to an audiologist
that specialized in tinnitus.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:41.384
He also did tests to make sure
that I didn't have a brain tumor

00:00:41.424 --> 00:00:45.783
or any of the other things I was
freaking out about and I was okay,

00:00:45.823 --> 00:00:49.976
but tinnitus is something
that you can't get rid of,

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:55.428
you have to learn to deal with and the
audiologist gave me all kinds of tips

00:00:55.468 --> 00:01:01.160
on how to add sound to my home to make
the tinnitus easier to deal with.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:06.451
So, at night, I listen to music
that I enjoy and it puts me in a good mood,

00:01:06.491 --> 00:01:12.680
I also exercise early in the evening so
I'm well and tired by the time I go to bed,

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:18.550
it's so much easier to sleep and just
being able to sleep better makes my life

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:23.639
so much better because dealing
with tinnitus is hard enough and being able

00:01:23.679 --> 00:01:29.580
to sleep and add sound to my home has
just really improved my quality of life.
